sdl2: report where files were dropped and when the pointer moves away

SDL2 drop events carry no position, but SDL3's do. The runtime's SDL2 is
sdl2-compat on SDL3, so when SDL3 is already loaded, add an SDL3 event
watch that remembers the last drop point, and report the drop with that
point and the window size. With a real SDL2 the drop is reported without
them, as before.

After a positioned drop, report the first pointer move of more than 4
pixels, a move into another window or leaving the window, once and only
within 30 seconds. The launcher uses it to skip dragging files into an app
the user has moved away from.

--- a/qapi/ui.json
+++ b/qapi/ui.json
@@ -1736,10 +1736,33 @@
